{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06FR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$W$", "MATH_0004": "$W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to W$", "MATH_0005": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-check-finite-type-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87955b6b44be14f27ae02579c55634c9110a1b1232924689b9913f16226d9a28", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fdffb3ad84fe2340f9e8b970d9983c5e93b7ef19d2cf8b63b13cf3fbe7f9feb4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a surjective, flat, and locally of finite\npresentation where <MATH_0003> is an algebraic space. If the base change\n<MATH_0004> is\nlocally of finite type, then <MATH_0005> is locally of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3476d76a1ad22c77a1fdc4e4f63df2a5dd7e9c22ec9acfcc80dde40452f273fb", "unit_id": "tag:06U7:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06FR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V$", "MATH_0002": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0006": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0007": "$U' = W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} U$", "MATH_0008": "$V' = W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} V$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{X}' = W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{Y}' = W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Y} = W$", "MATH_0011": "$U' \\to V' \\times_{\\mathcal{Y}'} \\mathcal{X}'$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{X}' \\to \\mathcal{Y}'$", "MATH_0013": "$U' \\to V'$", "MATH_0014": "$V' \\to V$", "MATH_0015": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0016": "$U \\to V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-descent-lemma-descending-property-locally-finite-type}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:82770a1fef5c9b1ea5e2d710d8661fe095d5eb583fd1029a16ae431dddd2d37f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60e1bb247d203fd10b1129d9aa7afebcb5f3ac33a0e35a67a6cc283176ca93b7", "source_text": "Choose an algebraic space <MATH_0001> and a surjective smooth morphism\n<MATH_0002>. Choose an algebraic space <MATH_0003> and a surjective\nsmooth morphism <MATH_0004>.\nWe have to show that <MATH_0005> is locally of finite presentation.\nNow we base change everything by <MATH_0006>: Set\n<MATH_0007>,\n<MATH_0008>,\n<MATH_0009>,\nand <MATH_0010>.\nThen it is still true that <MATH_0011>\nis smooth by base change. Hence by our definition of locally finite type\nmorphisms of algebraic stacks and the assumption that\n<MATH_0012> is locally of finite type,\nwe see that <MATH_0013> is locally of finite type. Then, since\n<MATH_0014> is surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation\nas a base change of <MATH_0015> we see that <MATH_0016> is\nlocally of finite type by\nDescent on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nand we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e627e8f3874c8e2ab46e2734dde91e98389862ccf8a9150c0e6d745c4ac7b4f9", "unit_id": "tag:06U7:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06FR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-check-finite-type-precompose}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dcd052d177e27930a6a0dd0c49c287570b732b7849d07937611fe07fd1f6c6ab", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:94fb0569015449f17d13eb7ad9480b0218cc27f35944c6b7140b800e002a83fb", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be morphisms of\nalgebraic stacks. Assume <MATH_0002> is locally of finite\ntype and that <MATH_0003> is representable by algebraic\nspaces, surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation.\nThen <MATH_0004> is locally of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dce702381c46e5f0d38a5d8807909356e539f9945cdedef32531de1ab62bdfc4", "unit_id": "tag:06U8:statement"}
